## 12. Project Success Criteria

The case study will be considered successfully completed when:

- The business problem and project objectives are clearly documented.
- Key stakeholders and their requirements are identified.
- Existing process gaps are documented.
- Business and functional requirements are traceable.
- Proposed process improvements are documented.
- User stories and acceptance criteria are prepared.
- UAT scenarios are defined.
- KPI-based recommendations are presented.

## 13. Conclusion

This project will apply Business Analysis practices to evaluate an IT service request management process and identify opportunities for operational improvement.

Through structured requirement documentation, process analysis, stakeholder identification and performance evaluation, the case study aims to demonstrate how a Business Analyst can translate business problems into clearly defined requirements and actionable recommendations.

